    "body": "## Motivation\nThe multimodal CPU preprocess pool defaults to `os.cpu_count()` workers, and a fork-started `ProcessPoolExecutor` forks them all on the first submit. On a 512-core host the first image request forks 512 processes and misses its timeout (seen as LLaVA test timeouts).\n\n## Modifications\n- `base_processor.py`: default `max_workers = min(os.cpu_count(), 16)`. `SGLANG_CPU_WORKERS` still overrides it.\n- New CPU unit test `test_base_processor_cpu_pool.py`: cap, small host, unknown CPU count, env override.\n\nThis changes the default on all backends, but only for hosts with more than 16 cores.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\nNo model-output change. LLaVA `test_vision_openai_server_a` video_images and multi_images pass on Arc Pro B60 (512-core host).\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\nFirst multimodal request on a 512-core host: no longer forks 512 workers (it was over the 10 s request timeout). Steady-state preprocessing uses at most 16 workers; set `SGLANG_CPU_WORKERS` for more.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41800285583](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41800285583)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41800285375](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41800285375)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41800285461](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41800285461)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test